Franco founded the MEIC (Ecclesial Movement for Cultural Commitment of Catholic Action) in the diocese and, with Maria Rosaria, took part in the 1995 ecclesial conference in Palermo, on returning from which he set out the lines of future pastoral commitment for all:
1. restoring legality and public morality;
2. promoting a social sense and a culture of participation;
3. deepening and developing Christian social teaching;
4. seeking new forms of solidarity economy
